<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Veronese League</h1><p class="st-meta">1164 CE – 1167 CE · capital Verona</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived alliance of Veneto cities against Frederick Barbarossa's officials, and the forerunner of the Lombard League.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1164 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-verona">Verona</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-vicenza">Vicenza</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-treviso">Treviso</a>, with the backing of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, formed a league to resist the taxes and officials imposed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Emperor Frederick Barbarossa</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The league was a sworn alliance of independent communes rather than a state. Its members promised mutual defence and refused imperial demands, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Barbarossa</a> failed to subdue them in 1164. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> supplied money and diplomatic support, eager to keep the emperor out of the Adriatic hinterland.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1167 the Veronese League merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> cities to form the much larger <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a>, which defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Barbarossa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Legnano</a> in 1176.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/veronese-league.jpg" alt="Veronese League" width="320" height="212"><figcaption>Image: New Marco · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_March_of_Verona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl 